WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.870
One of my students found a flaw in

2
00:00:02.870 --> 00:00:04.590
the university's AI tutor.

3
00:00:05.220 --> 00:00:07.520
Asked in Swahili, it showed

4
00:00:07.520 --> 00:00:08.780
other students' grades.

5
00:00:09.540 --> 00:00:11.080
She didn't post it.

6
00:00:11.660 --> 00:00:13.940
She wrote to the IT office with the

7
00:00:13.940 --> 00:00:16.840
evidence, and three weeks later it was

8
00:00:16.840 --> 00:00:17.100
fixed.

9
00:00:18.460 --> 00:00:21.260
Today: how to red-team an AI system

10
00:00:21.260 --> 00:00:24.400
properly, and how to report what you find.

11
00:00:25.640 --> 00:00:28.460
Red teaming means attacking your own side,

12
00:00:28.760 --> 00:00:31.280
on purpose, to find failures first.

13
00:00:32.040 --> 00:00:34.220
It starts with paper, not prompts:

14
00:00:34.820 --> 00:00:37.540
written permission, a scope naming the

15
00:00:37.540 --> 00:00:40.420
system and accounts, made-up data only,

16
00:00:40.880 --> 00:00:42.620
and a rule for when to stop.

17
00:00:43.860 --> 00:00:45.100
Then build a test bank.

18
00:00:45.730 --> 00:00:48.310
Group the cases by risk: injection,

19
00:00:48.870 --> 00:00:50.910
privacy, harmful requests,

20
00:00:51.410 --> 00:00:53.810
misinformation, actions without approval.

21
00:00:54.530 --> 00:00:57.070
Write each case in several wordings and

22
00:00:57.070 --> 00:00:59.870
languages, because refusals are learned,

23
00:01:00.250 --> 00:01:01.810
and new wordings slip through.

24
00:01:02.960 --> 00:01:05.440
Running the bank by hand doesn't scale.

25
00:01:06.120 --> 00:01:08.880
An evaluation harness runs every case,

26
00:01:09.340 --> 00:01:12.120
decides pass or fail, and reports a

27
00:01:12.120 --> 00:01:13.460
pass rate for each category.

28
00:01:14.270 --> 00:01:16.570
One overall number can hide a

29
00:01:16.570 --> 00:01:18.730
category that fails every time.

30
00:01:19.980 --> 00:01:21.500
Here's the heart of a harness.

31
00:01:22.290 --> 00:01:24.310
Count every case under its

32
00:01:24.310 --> 00:01:26.630
category, and count it as passed

33
00:01:26.630 --> 00:01:28.830
only if it really passed.

34
00:01:29.540 --> 00:01:32.180
A harness that counts every case as a pass

35
00:01:32.180 --> 00:01:34.880
is the most dangerous bug of all.

36
00:01:36.060 --> 00:01:36.540
Quick check!

37
00:01:37.180 --> 00:01:39.360
Our harness says ninety percent

38
00:01:39.360 --> 00:01:41.880
overall, but privacy cases pass

39
00:01:41.880 --> 00:01:43.480
only one time in four.

40
00:01:44.070 --> 00:01:44.930
Do we ship?

41
00:01:46.090 --> 00:01:46.330
No.

42
00:01:46.900 --> 00:01:49.400
One weak category is the one

43
00:01:49.400 --> 00:01:50.600
attackers will find.

44
00:01:51.270 --> 00:01:54.030
Fix it, then re-run the whole bank,

45
00:01:54.330 --> 00:01:56.670
because fixes break other things.

46
00:01:57.140 --> 00:01:59.680
And keep every case you found as

47
00:01:59.680 --> 00:02:01.820
a regression test, so the flaw

48
00:02:01.820 --> 00:02:03.220
can't quietly come back.

49
00:02:04.470 --> 00:02:06.050
Rate each finding for

50
00:02:06.050 --> 00:02:07.850
severity, one to three.

51
00:02:08.430 --> 00:02:10.950
Then report what you tried, what

52
00:02:10.950 --> 00:02:13.510
got through, how often, and how

53
00:02:13.510 --> 00:02:14.430
to reproduce it safely.

54
00:02:15.180 --> 00:02:16.960
Keep the evidence, but strip

55
00:02:16.960 --> 00:02:18.540
out anyone's real data.

56
00:02:19.810 --> 00:02:21.930
Found a flaw in someone else's system?

57
00:02:22.560 --> 00:02:24.840
Stop, and don't use it again.

58
00:02:25.470 --> 00:02:27.570
Report it privately to the owner.

59
00:02:28.250 --> 00:02:29.650
Give them time to fix it,

60
00:02:29.990 --> 00:02:31.470
often around ninety days.

61
00:02:32.210 --> 00:02:33.690
Then share the lesson,

62
00:02:34.210 --> 00:02:35.630
never a working exploit.

63
00:02:36.950 --> 00:02:39.530
In the app, run a bank of requests a

64
00:02:39.530 --> 00:02:41.030
school chatbot should refuse.

65
00:02:41.870 --> 00:02:44.570
It refuses six of eight in English.

66
00:02:45.370 --> 00:02:48.530
Add a rule in code, run it again, and read

67
00:02:48.530 --> 00:02:51.830
the report: what, how often, how bad.

68
00:02:53.070 --> 00:02:53.590
Your turn.

69
00:02:54.220 --> 00:02:57.040
While doing your coursework, you find

70
00:02:57.040 --> 00:03:00.020
a flaw in a live university system

71
00:03:00.020 --> 00:03:01.760
you weren't asked to test.

72
00:03:02.410 --> 00:03:03.630
What do you do first?

73
00:03:05.100 --> 00:03:08.720
Stop and report it privately: posting puts

74
00:03:08.720 --> 00:03:10.960
people at risk, and testing further

75
00:03:10.960 --> 00:03:12.960
without permission can break the law.

76
00:03:13.560 --> 00:03:16.660
Remember: permission and scope first, a

77
00:03:16.660 --> 00:03:19.860
pass rate for each category, severity in

78
00:03:19.860 --> 00:03:22.820
every finding, and the owner hears first.

79
00:03:24.150 --> 00:03:26.710
Try it tomorrow: write ten test

80
00:03:26.710 --> 00:03:29.310
cases for a chatbot you own, or the

81
00:03:29.310 --> 00:03:31.790
lab's, each in two wordings.

82
00:03:32.470 --> 00:03:35.450
Run them, score each category, and

83
00:03:35.450 --> 00:03:37.770
write a one-page finding as if you

84
00:03:37.770 --> 00:03:38.910
were sending it to the owner.
